From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xios <xios@localhost>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 00:15:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ios: register objc compiler in cross builds

mpv only enables Meson's Objective-C language after detecting a macOS SDK with
xcrun/xcodebuild. Those tools are not present in the Linux-to-iOS cross-build
container, so macos_sdk_version remains 0.0 and ao_audiounit.m fails with no
Objective-C compiler registered even though the cross file supplies objc.

Register Objective-C before the macOS SDK probe. The SDK-specific link flags
remain guarded by the existing macos_sdk_version block, so the cross build does
not pick up empty-path -isysroot flags.
---
 meson.build | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1495,3 +1495,5 @@ if macos_sdk_version != '0.0'
 endif
-
+
+add_languages('objc') # XIOS-force-objc
+
 xcrun = find_program('xcrun', required: get_option('swift-build').require(darwin))
